%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:cubic -- CUBIC reduces the window to 0.7 at a loss.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; TcpCubic is RFC 9438,
whose multiplicative decrease is 0.7.

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. This test separates TcpCubic: TcpNewReno, TcpReno, DcTcp and TcpTahoe set the threshold to
half the window or less, TcpWestwood to its estimate of the bandwidth, TcpVegas sets none at a
fast retransmit, and TcpNoCongestionControl and DumbTcp have no window.

Host under test: host1, without SACK, which sends 100000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and
the tap drops the 15th data segment once. Observation: level 2, the first slow-start threshold
is 0.7 of the largest window before the loss.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: cubic
%# value: "TcpCubic"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassCubic")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .captureMax("cwndBefore", "value")
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      double ratio = context.event.value / context.get("cwndBefore").doubleValue();
                      return ratio >= 0.62 && ratio <= 0.78;
                  })
                  .describe("the slow-start threshold at the loss, 0.7 of the window")
                  .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassCubic compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassCubic: PASS
